Subject: [PATCH] Qt: USCL_ROOM also names the console after the player

Games show the 3DS console name to the others (New Super Mario Bros. 2 lists
"Which Mario do you want to play with?" by it, "<name>'s Luigi has arrived!"),
and every Azahar was called "AZAHAR". With USCL_ROOM the player's name (first
10 characters, Unicode allowed) becomes the console username in the profile's
config savegame before the game starts.
---
--- a/src/citra_qt/citra_qt.cpp
+++ b/src/citra_qt/citra_qt.cpp
@@ -557,6 +557,14 @@
                             ? static_cast<char>(c.unicode())
                             : '_';
         nickname.resize(std::max<std::size_t>(nickname.size(), 4), '_');
+        // the console name the others see in games ("<name>'s Luigi"): the player's, 10 characters
+        if (const std::u16string name = spec.left(at).left(10).toStdU16String(); !name.empty()) {
+            const auto cfg = Service::CFG::GetModule(system);
+            if (cfg->GetUsername() != name) {
+                cfg->SetUsername(name);
+                cfg->UpdateConfigNANDSavegame();
+            }
+        }
         if (member && at >= 0 && colon > at) {
             member->Join(nickname, Service::CFG::GetConsoleIdHash(system),
                          spec.mid(at + 1, colon - at - 1).toStdString().c_str(),
-- 
